 abstract = {This paper applies the theory of granular computing to the load forecasting model of electric power systems. By constructing the electric load data as a fuzzy extension set, the concepts of detectors and sample spaces reconstructed in primitive form are proposed. The biological thinking of the complement system is used to optimize the dependent function, and a comprehensive forecasting model is established to evaluate and combine multiple forecasting results, achieving the complementary advantages of various models. The experiments show that the proposed forecasting model effectively improves the adaptability and accuracy of the electric power system, and has broad prospects for application in the field of load forecasting.},
