 abstract = {Parking occupancy has been a prevalent issue in the city of Kuala Lumpur especially in busy areas such as commerce areas. An individual can spend a ridiculous amount of time attempting to find parking occupancy and may still end up not finding a parking space. The cause of this is due to the rapid urbanization within the city which leads to not only the increase in population, but also the increase in vehicles owned, more vehicles means more spaces are required for parking. As such, trying to find parking occupancy has been a tantamount issue. This research aims to alleviate such issues via parking occupancy detection with image recognition. The proposed model used for this research is You Only Look Once (YOLO). YOLO is used here to classify parking occupancy on the datasets discovered on Roboflow, and its performance is evaluated using mAP50, mAP50-95 and confusion matrix. The outcome of the YOLO model utilized in this research attained an overall mAP50 of 94.5% and an overall mAP50-95 of 63.8%.},
