 abstract = {Given the pervasive presence of metaphors in language, the task of processing metaphors holds significant importance within the domain of natural language processing. Such proposals for the automatic processing of metaphors range from a hand-coded rule system to deep learning techniques. The initial stage in the process of metaphor comprehension, often regarded as the most challenging, involves Pre-processing stage for metaphor identification then Feature extraction, Metaphor Identification, Classification, Interpretation and Evaluation. In this paper, we provide an overview of the theoretical foundations of metaphors, as well as the various models and practical applications that have been suggested for computational metaphor processing, including the tasks of metaphor detection and comprehension. We suggested an approach for computational metaphor processing using large language models.},
