 abstract = {Real-time healthcare process optimization is the practice of optimizing processes in 4IR-based product and service organizations, focusing on using real-time data collected through advanced technologies like AI. Continuous monitoring and analyzing of data to drive decisions Process adjustments in real-time Real-time optimization of health care processes using AI-powered decision support systems Such systems use machine learning and other AI-based algorithms to process enormous volumes of data from disparate sources like electronic health records, medical devices, and patient-generated inputs. They can alert healthcare practitioners of areas needing real-time attention and inform evaluation classification and process optimization. AI-driven decision support systems are used for real-time optimization and can spot patterns & predict outputs. They do their job by studying the pattern; such systems can constantly analyze data. In turn, these will lead to machine learning outcomes that could help identify something wrong and inefficiency in a health care process, so it gives recommendations that think tanks probably won},
